  "conditions": {
    "dedicated": true,
    "detail": "Box dedicated to this run. The qwen-image-spark server on :8020 is the lane under test and the only process holding the GPU; no second engine, no compile, no desktop session. Ambient temperature unknown (no sensor on this box).",
    "isolation_check": "nvidia-smi --query-compute-apps listed exactly one pid (the :8020 uvicorn worker) before and during the run; pgrep found no sglang, vllm, comfy or sd-cli process. A 1 Hz sampler recorded the sum of --query-compute-apps and free -m for the whole run."
  },
  "gotchas": [
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "nvidia-smi --query-gpu=memory.used returns [N/A] on GB10: the CPU and the GPU share one pool and the per-device counter is not implemented. vram_peak_gb here comes from the sum of --query-compute-apps=used_memory instead, which the harness now falls back to. It is a whole-device figure and it is only equal to this lane's footprint because the box ran nothing else."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "The model name on the wire is not the Hugging Face repo id. This server's build_job lowercases the model field and checks it against {\"\", \"qwen-image-2.1\", \"qwen-image\", \"qwen\", \"gpt-image-1\", \"dall-e-3\", \"dall-e-2\"}, so a packet that sends Qwen/Qwen-Image-2.1 gets a 400 on every request. The packet carries served_model_id=qwen-image-2.1."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "Effective guidance was 1.0, the lane's own default: guidance_scale is a per-request field, not a QIMG_ variable, and build_job falls back to 1.0 when neither guidance_scale nor true_cfg_scale is sent. The workloads send neither, so args carries no guidance and the number to compare against another lane is 1.0. Above 1.0 this pipeline runs a second transformer forward per step, which roughly doubles seconds per image."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "Seconds per image are the server's own timing.total_ms (queue/encode/denoise/decode), not the HTTP wall clock; the harness prefers it for this engine. On the smoke render the two were 53.432 s and 53.45 s, so the client costs ~20 ms."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "QIMG_MAX_PIXELS defaults to 4300800 in 0.1.1 (it was 4227072 in 0.1.0). Every shape these suites ask for fits: 2048x2048 is 4194304 and 2752x1536 is 4227072. On 0.1.0 the 2752x1536 adherence and fidelity cases would have been refused with a 400."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "This lane renders 1024x1024 at 40 steps within a 0.21 s band over 17 independent cases (52.83-53.04 s), so its percentiles are narrow by construction and a p90/p50 gap here means a shape change, not variance. 2048x2048 costs 251.5 s, 4.75x the 1K time for 4x the pixels; one reference image adds ~6 s and a second ~8 s more."
    }
  ],
